{
  "title": "Claude Sessions",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "581afc6a799a9dcf",
      "text": "Every Claude Code session running on this laptop, read live from `claude agents`. Opened from \u25c9 on a plan's status line, where that plan's sessions come first."
    },
    {
      "type": "plan",
      "id": "96edaedf0ffd1811",
      "text": "SESSIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "9efa24f71ff61e59",
      "text": "# Reading the list\n> Waiting first, then working."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "380979025d614da2",
      "text": "*Waiting for you* means the session has stopped for you, often at a permission prompt or a question: open it and answer. *Working* means it is thinking or running a tool. *At its prompt* means it has finished and waits for your next message."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "91afbc8273d6d0f8",
      "text": "A session the wiki started is named after its plan and its phase, and has *open \u2197*, which opens it full screen in a new tab. A session with no link was started in the Claude app or in a terminal window. Terminal sessions with no Claude in them are listed under the table, folded."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "94e6f6043b607b23",
      "text": "The list is read through the terminal service on this laptop, so it shows only on a page opened on the laptop. It refreshes every 15 seconds while the page is open. [[Claude in Wiki]] says how the sessions start and how to answer them."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "82a9ce549b3e6f15",
      "text": "# See\n\n- [[Claude in Wiki]]\n- [[Plan Tool]]\n- [[About Plan Plugin]]"
    }
  ],
